- Root `.nvmrc`: `24.19.0`. Frontend/backend/desktop package files: `"engines": { "node": "24.19.0" }` and `"packageManager": "pnpm@12.6.0"`.
- pnpm only; not npm, yarn, or bun. Maintain frontend/backend/desktop `pnpm-lock.yaml` and include them when commits are authorised, not `package-lock.json`.
- `frontend/.npmrc`, `backend/.npmrc`, and `desktop/.npmrc`: `save-exact=true`. Pin package versions without range operators.
- New projects and imported feature code match the table. Convert incompatible lock files and align versions before accepting imported code.
- Do not replace the fixed frameworks, API library, styling, ORM, or database without owner agreement. Additional libraries are pinned and recorded in `docs/Dependencies.md` with reasons; material additions need owner approval.
- Keep ESLint on 9.x until relevant plugins are checked for compatibility with 10; obtain agreement and update the guide before changing that standard.
- Frontend uses `eslint-config-next`; backend and desktop use `typescript-eslint`. Each has `eslint.config.mjs`.
- One root `.prettierrc` serves all three packages. Imported code uses it; remove duplicate formatting configurations.
- Run lint and formatting checks before merging. A disabled lint rule needs a recorded reason; no blanket file-level `eslint-disable`.

- Electron supplies its own embedded runtime; local Next.js/NestJS servers and tooling use installed Node.js 24.19.0. Check actual executable/version resolution before changing tooling. Use installed pnpm 12.6.0 directly; do not recreate .tools/bootstrap scripts/pnpm wrappers without owner agreement.
- Electron is approved for the desktop host, not as a replacement frontend/backend. See desktop-electron.mdc. Pin/document additional packages and allow only identified dependency build scripts.

## Approved localization/auth additions

- i18next 26.4.2, react-i18next 17.0.16, bcrypt 6.0.0, and @types/bcrypt 6.0.0 are approved translation/password dependencies. jest-environment-jsdom 30.5.2 supports frontend DOM tests. Pin/document all; no online provider or second auth framework.
